---
title: Grilled branzino with Greek lemon sauce
servings: 2
yield: 1 whole fish
tags: [greek, grill, summer, weekend]
cuisine: greek
source: Best Grilled Whole Branzino with Greek Fish Sauce, Food52, https://food52.com/recipes/36592-best-grilled-whole-branzino-with-greek-fish-sauce
---

Season the @branzino{1}(whole, scaled and gutted) inside and out with @salt{} and @black pepper{}. Fill the cavity with the @oregano{2%sprigs} and @lemon{1}(sliced), and rub the skin with @olive oil{}.

For the sauce, mix the juice of @lemon{1}, @olive oil{1/2%cup}, @oregano{1/4%cup}(roughly chopped) and @garlic{1%clove}(lightly smashed). Season with @salt{} and @ground black pepper{} and let it sit while the fish cooks.

Heat a #grill{} to medium-high. Grill the fish ~{5%minutes} a side, until the flesh is opaque and flakes from the bone. A #fish basket{} makes turning it easy.

Serve with the sauce and another @lemon{1}(sliced).

> Lemon to oil is a matter of taste; about one part lemon to three of oil is a good start.
